{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122551","id":4306596408,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABALFyOA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122551","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122551.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122551.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122551","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122551/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122551/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122551/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/7b1ea79f9df19b90127e2701669299429120b4ed","number":122551,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Move collection literal type adjustments to dedicated helper","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Code cleanup in the GDScript Analyzer\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nWe usually analyze inside-out, so e.g. a call analyzes its parameters and after that we analyzer the call.\r\n\r\nFor collection literals we do an outside-in update pass, so that a collection literal can appear in contexts were a typed collection is expected (usually collection literals produce untyped collection).\r\n\r\nThis outside-in update pass always requires a lot of validity checks:\r\n- is this a collection literal? \r\n- is the type expected in this context a typed collection?\r\n- does the expected collection type match the literal type? (we actually did not do that check previously which could lead to somewhat confusing error messages)\r\n\r\nAnd after all that is check we still need to distinguish the collection type to choose the right update implementation.\r\n\r\nAll of this adds repetitive branching to methods that are already complex enough. This PR bundles those validity checks into a new helper function with a descriptive name, which replaces all the duplicated check and call procedures across the analyzer.\r\n\r\nIn addition the PR gets rid of some premature optimization in `reduce_call`. When we did the original inside-out pass we would already check whether some call parameters are collection literals. We would store this info and use it later to do potential updates. The catch: there are ~300LOC between initializing those collections and actually using them. Given that parameter counts usually are low I think we can just iterate over all parameters again and do the check whether the param is a collection as needed. The long lifetime of those helper collections just adds mental overhead to one our most complicated functions.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":""